  "label": "The man with blood is mapped as the speaker of the joke",
  "description": "The visual of the distressed man with blood is mapped onto the textual entity 'my wife asked me where i'd like to be buried', implying that the man is the 'me' in the question. The text sets up a scenario where the speaker (the man) is being asked a serious question, and his subsequent inappropriate response is the punchline. The visual of the man's distress and injury serves as the embodiment of the speaker who is caught in the absurd and taboo situation described in the text.",
